# Supabase — client-side configuration
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and replace the placeholder values with your
# real project credentials:
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# `.env.local` is git-ignored and must never be committed.
#
# Only variables prefixed with `VITE_` are exposed to the browser by Vite.
# Never put the Supabase service-role key in a VITE_* variable — it would be
# bundled into the public client build. Service-role keys belong exclusively in
# server-side environments.
#
# Find these values in your Supabase dashboard under Project Settings → API.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional — local verification only. Not read by the app, never bundled.
#
# `scripts/probes/phase4-admin-probes.cjs` uses these to prove three things it
# cannot prove anonymously: that a signed-in non-admin is refused, that a
# signed-in admin is allowed, and that receipt signed URLs work end to end.
# Leave them blank and those sections report SKIP rather than PASS.
#
# Create both accounts in the Supabase Dashboard (Authentication → Users → Add
# user) with "Auto Confirm User" ticked. Link ONLY the admin one into
# public.admins using supabase/maintenance/grant_admin.sql — the second account
# must stay out of that table, since being a non-admin is what it tests.
#
# These are test accounts on a development project. Do not reuse a real
# password here, and do not add these keys to any deployed environment.

PROBE_ADMIN_EMAIL=
PROBE_ADMIN_PASSWORD=
PROBE_NONADMIN_EMAIL=
PROBE_NONADMIN_PASSWORD=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Edge Function secrets — NOT read from this file, listed here as documentation.
#
# These four belong to supabase/functions/send-email, the only component that
# talks to a mail provider. They are set on the deployed function and never
# read from any .env file, so putting real values here would achieve nothing
# except committing them:
#
#   supabase secrets set RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxx
#   supabase secrets set EMAIL_DISPATCH_SECRET="$(openssl rand -hex 32)"
#   supabase secrets set EMAIL_FROM="Drizzypips <noreply@yourdomain.com>"
#   supabase secrets set PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://yourdomain.com
#
# None of them is prefixed VITE_, and none ever may be. A VITE_ variable is
# inlined into the public client build, so a VITE_RESEND_API_KEY would hand the
# ability to send mail as this brand to every visitor who opened devtools. The
# frontend has no email capability at all by design: it can only ask a database
# function to enqueue a row, and this Edge Function is what delivers it.
#
#   RESEND_API_KEY         the mail provider credential.
#   EMAIL_DISPATCH_SECRET  what stops the function's public URL being an open
#                          relay. Sent as the x-dispatch-secret header and
#                          checked before anything else happens. Generate it
#                          randomly; it is not a password anyone types.
#   EMAIL_FROM             a sender on a domain verified with Resend. Without
#                          verification, delivery silently degrades to spam.
#   PUBLIC_SITE_URL        where the buttons in the emails point.
#
# SUPABASE_URL and SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY are injected into the Edge runtime
# by the platform. Do not set them by hand, and never copy the service-role key
# into this file.
